-- title:
--   Langlands reciprocity conjecture for $\mathrm{GL}(n)$ over number fields
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $K$ is a number field, $G_K=\mathrm{Gal}(\bar K/K)$ its absolute Galois group with the Krull topology, and $\mathbb A_K$ its adele ring. An **Artin representation** is a continuous homomorphism $\rho: G_K\to\mathrm{GL}_n(\mathbb C)$. We say $\rho$ is **automorphic** if there are a nonzero bounded cusp form $\varphi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_n(\mathbb A_K)$ with unitary central character and a finite set $S$ of primes of $K$ such that for every prime $\mathfrak p\notin S$: $\rho$ is unramified at $\mathfrak p$, $\varphi$ is right invariant under $\mathrm{GL}_n(\mathcal O_{\mathfrak p})$, and
--   $$T_{\mathfrak p,i}\,\varphi \;=\; N\mathfrak p^{\,i(n-i)/2}\,e_i\big(\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_{\mathfrak p})\big)\,\varphi\qquad(1\le i\le n),$$
--   where $T_{\mathfrak p,i}$ is the Hecke operator of the double coset of $\mathrm{diag}(\varpi,\dots,\varpi,1,\dots,1)$ ($i$ entries $\varpi$) and $e_i(\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_{\mathfrak p}))$ is the $i$-th elementary symmetric function of the eigenvalues of an arithmetic Frobenius. Equivalently, the cuspidal automorphic representation generated by $\varphi$ has the same local $L$-factors as $\rho$ at all $\mathfrak p\notin S$.
--
--   **Conjecture.** Let $\rho:G_K\to\mathrm{GL}_n(\mathbb C)$ be a continuous irreducible representation. Then $\rho$ is automorphic: there is a cuspidal automorphic representation $\pi$ of $\mathrm{GL}_n(\mathbb A_K)$ with
--   $$L_{\mathfrak p}(s,\pi)=L_{\mathfrak p}(s,\rho)=\det\big(1-\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_{\mathfrak p})N\mathfrak p^{-s}\big)^{-1}\quad\text{for almost all }\mathfrak p.$$
--
--   This is Langlands' reciprocity conjecture: every Artin $L$-function of an irreducible representation is the $L$-function of a cuspidal automorphic representation of $\mathrm{GL}(n)$. It implies Artin's conjecture that $L(s,\rho)$ is entire for nontrivial irreducible $\rho$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Irreducibility is required: for reducible $\rho$ the matching automorphic representation is an isobaric sum, not cuspidal. The conjecture is stated in its standard form, with matching of local factors at almost all primes.
-- source:
--   Langlands program (Wikipedia article, uploaded PDF), section Reciprocity and section Status; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Langlands_program; R. P. Langlands, Problems in the theory of automorphic forms, LNM 170 (1970), https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0079065

import Definitions.Def_LanglandsReciprocity_defs
import Mathlib

namespace LanglandsReciprocity

open NumberField

/-- **Goal (Langlands reciprocity conjecture for `GL(n)`).** Every irreducible
`n`-dimensional Artin representation of a number field `K` is automorphic: some cuspidal
automorphic form on `GL(n, 𝔸_K)` has the same local `L`-factors as `ρ` at almost all primes. -/
theorem reciprocity_conjecture (K : Type*) [Field K] [NumberField K] (n : ℕ)
    (ρ : Gal(AlgebraicClosure K/K) →* GL (Fin n) ℂ) (hρ : Continuous ρ)
    (hirr : IsIrreducible ρ) :
    IsAutomorphic ρ := by sorry

end LanglandsReciprocity
